{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance","id":466822,"title":"Getting Harmony into Balance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T18:57:00-07:00","id":466822,"title":"Getting Harmony into Balance","content":"So I was thinking about Harmony the other day after posting in the Low Harmony thread. Reading over what happens when your Harmony gets to 3 (as low as you start out high) made me realize just how bad being out of balance with Harmony can suck. The sweet spot is super sweet with no extra Kuruth triggers at all at 5 and all shifting being free and reflexive. 4 and 6 are not so bad as your shifting is still free and you only have to deal with your specific (and thereby avoidable) triggers. At 3 and 7 your shifting gets either out of control or hard to do, which stinks.<br /> Luckily, at 3, you also pick up those extra few break-towards-flesh points, such as eating processed food or spending a mere day without going into the Hisil. For some reason, 8 is the threshold for relatively-easy-to-hit breaking points on the break towards spirit side. As such, you have to do something serious to hit that first breaking point.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my point. Being as the change from 7 to 6 Harmony is almost entirely beneficial, and the 6 to 5 one moreso, is there any reason you would ever want to succeed on your first two breaking point rolls? As such, do you need to make them?<br /> I went back and checked the most basic &quot;when to roll dice&quot; rules, and they said &quot;When your character\u2019s trying to accomplish something&quot;. Chances seem good that if you are hitting a breaking point that would swing your towards the middle, you did it deliberately to indulge that half of your nature. If you aren't trying to resist the pull of your other half, should you roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:32:06-07:00","id":466884,"title":"","content":"You should still roll. Think about it, if you could just concede a Breaking Point roll, no one with Harmony above 5 would ever actually roll on a Breaking Point towards spirit, and no one below 5 would ever roll on a Breaking Point towards flesh. It just makes it too easy to maintain balanced harmony, which is <i>supposed</i> to be a struggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:35:48-07:00","id":466889,"title":"","content":"I think you should roll. The fact that you can't spend Willpower to modify the roll suggests that it's really out your character's hands. Like with Integrity, you don't choose how you react, you react and then try to make sense out of the reaction. Harmony is different, for obvious reasons, and I'd say it's even less &quot;controllable&quot; than Integrity, since breaking toward spirit has less to do with your psyche and more to do with your spirit purging its tethers to the world of flesh.<br /> <br /> However, you might allow an exceptional success on <i>any </i>Breaking Point to be exchanged for a normal failure. The character has a moment of <i>satori</i> and finds the balance he's been seeking, and sheds either the bonds of Flesh or the essence of Spirit without regret or rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:46:49-07:00","id":466899,"title":"","content":"Your character shouldn't be as aware of the mechanical aspects of things, I don't think. You could certainly cheer them on to fail, but the failures and successes of your character shouldn't be entirely within your control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:49:32-07:00","id":466902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=466889#post466889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, you might allow an exceptional success on <i>any </i>Breaking Point to be exchanged for a normal failure. The character has a moment of <i>satori</i> and finds the balance he's been seeking, and sheds either the bonds of Flesh or the essence of Spirit without regret or rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool idea, actually. I may steal that for my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T20:26:24-07:00","id":466926,"title":"","content":"Also worth remembering that at the thresholds where you pick up extra Breaking Points you also <i>lose access to the Touchstone that helps you rebalance.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:52:31-07:00","id":467219,"title":"","content":"Ooh! That's a good amount of response for this.<br /> <br /> @Satchel: You pick up the easy-rider BTF points at 3, but lose the Physical Touhcstone at 2. What you say is true on the other side, though, which makes me think the 3 was another errata on the breaking points chart on top of the formatting error. Unless you're supposed to get the easy ones (leading Siskur-Dah etc.) at 7 instead of 8...<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin &amp; Verge: I really really like that idea, too. I'll probably bring this whole issue up with my group, the exceptional success point included.<br /> <br /> @nofather: To the character its a question of the pull of their nature. They can feel that one side of them is calling but being ignored, and they hit the breaking point because they are responding to that. As such, the roll to resist heading towards the middle seems like a roll to see if that side of their nature was out to lunch when you tried responding.<br /> <br /> @just Charlaquin: At the points where you wouldn't want to fail, so long as your Touchstone isn't dead or broken, your dice pool will be Resolve + Composure + 2. Unless you took a 1 in either resistance stat, you'll have at least 6 dice. 6 dice have a really good chance of getting one success, so you need to do something really bad to have a chance for it to move at all. This seems out of keeping with the &quot;your Harmony could fluctuate wildly during play&quot; assertion. The mechanics of it do make it hard to resist the slide away form balance, which makes sense to me. They also make it hard to accept the call towards it. That side of it makes less sense. It's the same roll you're making at every breaking point - why would you sometimes want it to succeed and sometimes want it to fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:35:51-07:00","id":467306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467219#post467219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@nofather: To the character its a question of the pull of their nature. They can feel that one side of them is calling but being ignored, and they hit the breaking point because they are responding to that. As such, the roll to resist heading towards the middle seems like a roll to see if that side of their nature was out to lunch when you tried responding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmony is not their nature, however. That's why they strive for it. As a composite of two types of being so drastically different, their nature is disharmony. And even then, not all Werewolves want Harmony with their spirit side. Some reject it altogether, grasping for Harmony 10 and to be pulled 'out of the game.' The Fire-Touched and other more spiritually inclined may prefer a low Harmony, after all, you are no longer human, why should you pretend that you are?<br /> <br /> Though I did like Verge's idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:47:51-07:00","id":467316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467306#post467306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harmony is not their nature, however. That's why they strive for it. As a composite of two types of being so drastically different, their nature is disharmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got something of a good point with disharmony being the nature of the beast. Harmony is an understood and in-game concept, though. In the Bone Shadows-to-Iron Masters steryotype, they call it out. I think it's in the section on Touchstones that they specifically say it is out-of-game jargon to call one that. As such, the concept of Harmony is something Uratha think about and talk about.<br /> Sure, you're not human, but you are of two worlds. Your Hishu form is just as natural and part of who you are as your Urhan or Gauru forms. The Fire-Touched are crazy to ignore that fact. Also, they're Rabid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:00:09-07:00","id":467328,"title":"","content":"&quot;Harmony&quot; is an in-game concept. &quot;Harmony 5&quot; is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:17:56-07:00","id":467345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467328#post467328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Harmony&quot; is an in-game concept. &quot;Harmony 5&quot; is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. But if Harmony is known, Balanced Harmony would also be known, even if it isn't known as 5. You, as a Uratha, would be able to feel how relatively out of balance you are.<br /> My proposition, overall, is that you can always choose to fail. From a player standpoint, especially if you're a player trying to reach balance, you would only choose to fail rolls that would lead you to 5. From a character standpoint, the idea would be &quot;I'm not feeling properly harmonious and I'm indulging the side that's been deglected&quot;. As you commit the acts that ressonate with your spirit or flesh half, you just agree with the ressonance instead of saying &quot;no! I may have done that thing, but that's not who I am.&quot;<br /> This actually seems kinda similar to the low-harmony auto-shifting question. If you feel the need to run and you want to run, do you have to take the slow route from Hishu to Urhan that goes through Dalu and maybe some other things? Or can you just do what feels right? In that case, the form resisting your instincts takes is only shifting certain aspects of yourself per turn rather than going all the way at once. In this case, resisting the urge means rolling, because maybe you just can't.<br /> <br /> Edit: I just realized that I didn't finish my initial thought. Being as you could always have the option to fail outright, if your character wasn't after balanced harmony, all they'd have to do is really commit to doing things that were breaking points towards whichever side they wanted to emphasize (which generally involve denying the other side).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-03-2015, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:18:48-07:00","id":467407,"title":"","content":"That just makes it way too easy to sculpt your Harmony to what ever value you want. Maintaining a certain level of Harmony (especially balanced Harmony) should be a struggle, and if all you have to do is seek out a single breaking point in the appropriate direction and chose to fail it, no one will ever be off their preferred number for longer than a session. It actually precludes &quot;shifting wildly&quot; even more that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:27:47-07:00","id":467482,"title":"","content":"Should you not be able to pursue the Harmony you desire, though?<br /> If you WANT to be More Human, should you not have that choice? If you want to be more spirit, should you also not have that choice? Yes, some may take advantage to stay in the sweet spot, but you will always have things that push one way or the other. Has choice been completely eliminated from the equation? If so, I see that as a bad change rather than something that facilitates drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:35:00-07:00","id":467521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467482#post467482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should you not be able to pursue the Harmony you desire, though?<br /> If you WANT to be More Human, should you not have that choice? If you want to be more spirit, should you also not have that choice? Yes, some may take advantage to stay in the sweet spot, but you will always have things that push one way or the other. Has choice been completely eliminated from the equation? If so, I see that as a bad change rather than something that facilitates drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pursue whatever Harmony you want, that's not what the argument is.<br /> <br /> The argument is that maintaining Harmony at <i>whatever level you choose</i> should not be so trivial as to just be able to fail a breaking point. There must be a chance that what you (as a player) want doesn't occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:53:37-07:00","id":467539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467482#post467482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should you not be able to pursue the Harmony you desire, though?<br /> If you WANT to be More Human, should you not have that choice? If you want to be more spirit, should you also not have that choice? Yes, some may take advantage to stay in the sweet spot, but you will always have things that push one way or the other. Has choice been completely eliminated from the equation? If so, I see that as a bad change rather than something that facilitates drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Breaking Points are things that can be actively sought out and/or consciously avoided. You can sever ties with one of your Touchstones to make falling in the opposite direction easier. Or or better yet, take the Merit that increases the bonus from one Touchstone and decreases the bonus from the other. There are plenty of things you can do to pursue higher or lower Harmony, you're not completely without choice in the matter. But you shouldn't be able to to just pick any specific dot rating you want and maintain it effortlessly. Allowing you to chose to auto-fail Breaking Point rolls makes that not only possible, but trivially easy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe an example will help communicate my objection more clearly. Let's say I'm playing in a game that uses this rule, and I want to have Harmony 4, because I like the essence-free reflexive shifting, but for roleplaying purposes I don't want to eliminate my specific Death Rage trigger and I think it's fitting for my character to be more on the spirit side than the flesh side. All I would have to do is take Father's Form and the Totemic Empowerment Rite at character creation. Over the next three days, I use Totemic Empowerment each day, triggering a Breaking Point towards Spirit each time and &quot;choosing to fail&quot; those rolls. Now I'm at Harmony 4. If I ever gain Harmony, I can use Totemic Empowerment again and chose to fail the roll. If I ever lose Harmony, I can shift to Gauru and back out of it without entering combat, triggering a Breaking Point towards Flesh and chose to fail the roll. I am now, for all intents and purposes, permanently at Harmony 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:55:39-07:00","id":467611,"title":"","content":"To add something else to the suggestion: I feel it was an unfortunate choice to base the dice pool on Resolve + Composure. It creates this strange situation that Werewolves can benefit from having a low Willpower (perhaps unique among the denizens of the World of Darkness), as this makes their Harmony more malleable. In the long run a low Res + Comp score makes it easier to stay around Harmony 6 to 4 through Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are lots of downsides to having a low Res + Comp score, but it still does not feel it is working as intended. I am also having a hard time understanding why it is that dice pool from a narrative and in-universe perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:20:57-07:00","id":467636,"title":"","content":"Breaking one way or the other is a shift in one's psyche. Of course it would be resisted by their stubbornness attributes. Your willpower is a measure of how hard you can put your foot down and tell the world &quot;no, <i>you</i> move&quot; Changing one's outlook is something that needs to get past that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:22:54-07:00","id":467638,"title":"","content":"Not to mention having a high Willpower also means that you can <i>stay</i> at your desired Harmony level more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:30:46-07:00","id":467672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467611#post467611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add something else to the suggestion: I feel it was an unfortunate choice to base the dice pool on Resolve + Composure. It creates this strange situation that Werewolves can benefit from having a low Willpower (perhaps unique among the denizens of the World of Darkness), as this makes their Harmony more malleable. In the long run a low Res + Comp score makes it easier to stay around Harmony 6 to 4 through Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are lots of downsides to having a low Res + Comp score, but it still does not feel it is working as intended. I am also having a hard time understanding why it is that dice pool from a narrative and in-universe perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it six of one and half a dozen of the other? Low Willpower allows you to more easily maintain balanced Harmony by breaking in the correct direction more often, but also makes it harder by breaking in the incorrect direction more often. High Willpower makes it easier to maintain high harmony by breaking in the wrong direction less often, but also makes it harder by breaking in the correct direction less often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:42:59-07:00","id":467689,"title":"","content":"@Charlaquin: In your example, having the roll be necessary every time would only make the process take more time, and that only in the breaking towards spirit direction. The person determined to become fleshy by flaunting The Father's Form would, mechanically speaking, have no trouble doing it. Fail a roll? Try again 6 seconds later. The Totemic Empowerment one lasts until sunrise, so that one would be once a day. That said, being a little high on the Flesh side is less severe of a problem than being a little on the low side, so a few extra days might not be a big deal.<br /> <br /> BigDamnHero brings up a good point, though, that the whole idea of having dice is so the player doesn't automatically get everything they want. My point is that dice rolls are typically there to make that happen. In this case, though, a good roll is a bad thing, which seems a little backwards.<br /> Maybe there should always be a roll. But maybe players should declare their intended or hoped-for harmony in advance and rolls towards it should NEED success to break whereas rolls away from it should require success to stay put. Were that the case, then The-Willpower-Pool would still make sense as the dice pool for this roll.<br /> saibot commented that, as it stands, Resolve + Composure doesn't make sense for this. If you're rolling that pool to resist a change you're hoping to give in to, then where is this bubble of will coming from? Then it becomes more the Personal-Inertia pool than the actual Willpower pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:56:39-07:00","id":467700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467689#post467689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BigDamnHero brings up a good point, though, that the whole idea of having dice is so the player doesn't automatically get everything they want. My point is that dice rolls are typically there to make that happen. In this case, though, a good roll is a bad thing, which seems a little backwards.<br /> Maybe there should always be a roll. But maybe players should declare their intended or hoped-for harmony in advance and rolls towards it should NEED success to break whereas rolls away from it should require success to stay put. Were that the case, then The-Willpower-Pool would still make sense as the dice pool for this roll.<br /> saibot commented that, as it stands, Resolve + Composure doesn't make sense for this. If you're rolling that pool to resist a change you're hoping to give in to, then where is this bubble of will coming from? Then it becomes more the Personal-Inertia pool than the actual Willpower pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work better than allowing the choice to take a failure, I think.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the tension caused by the fact that the kind of dice pool you want to have varies with your Harmony. With this suggestion, a higher dice pool is always better. There's no drive to go to extremes of physical or spiritual behavior to incur harsher penalties on your Breaking Points. There's no temptation to murder one of your own touchstones so they're not holding you back from achieving balance. That's a lot of potential drama lost. I like that what will help you achieve balance one day, may come back around to bite you when you can no longer stop yourself from falling/rising too far, and successful rolls always giving the preferable result doesn't allow that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:10:04-07:00","id":467721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467636#post467636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breaking one way or the other is a shift in one's psyche. Of course it would be resisted by their stubbornness attributes. Your willpower is a measure of how hard you can put your foot down and tell the world &quot;no, <i>you</i> move&quot; Changing one's outlook is something that needs to get past that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we go with this argument than Detachement in Vampire should also be Resolve + Composure: &quot;I won't let go of my human attachements, damnit!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> @BigDamnHero &amp; Charlaquin: Fair enough, but you need to get there first. It creates this situation that rewards raising your Resolve and Composure depending on where your Harmony currently is, which just seems like a really odd mechanic to me.<br /> <br /> I also imagine this really weird scenario of an old Werewolf, who had been really set in his ways and had very high or low Harmony... but now something happened that made him have a change of heart. He actually <b>wants</b> to become more balanced... but his own great Resolve is somehow an obstacle to him? His own high Composure makes him too unruly to achieve it? Even the most severe Breaking Points are &quot;only&quot; a -3, which is not that much when compared to a high-end Willpower score.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:19:59-07:00","id":467731,"title":"","content":"If someone became invested in moving towards one side over another, they would likely focus on a touchstone by taking the Anchored merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:25:34-07:00","id":467740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467721#post467721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we go with this argument than Detachement in Vampire should also be Resolve + Composure: &quot;I won't let go of my human attachements, damnit!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I found it pretty weird that Humanity Breaking Points weren't based on Resolve + Composure with a modifier based on your current Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467721#post467721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@BigDamnHero &amp; Charlaquin: Fair enough, but you need to get there first. It creates this situation that rewards raising your Resolve and Composure depending on where your Harmony currently is, which just seems like a really odd mechanic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't speak for anyone but myself, but I find that to be a feature, and a big one, not a bug. At character creation, you want to start with a lower Willpower. You want to start with a spiritual Touchstone but not a physical one. You may even want that Merit that increases your bonus from one Touchstone at the cost of the other. Once you hit 5 though, those decisions could backfire on you. You might end up dropping pretty far towards spirit, and need to start taking extreme measures to recover the balance. But you'd better be careful not to over-correct! That back-and forth tension, those dynamic incentives that vary based on how far you are to either side, to me that is exactly what the Harmony balancing act is all about!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467721#post467721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also imagine this really weird scenario of an old Werewolf, who had been really set in his ways and had very high or low Harmony... but now something happened that made him have a change of heart. He actually <b>wants</b> to become more balanced... but his own great Resolve is somehow an obstacle to him? His own high Composure makes him too unruly to achieve it? Even the most severe Breaking Points are &quot;only&quot; a -3, which is not that much when compared to a high-end Willpower score.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is admittedly a little counter-intuitive. I agree there may have been a better way to calculate the base dice pool. That said, it's only the sample Breaking Points that cap out at -3. The ST can always create new Breaking Points and/or apply additional penalties based on the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2015, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:51:00-07:00","id":467843,"title":"","content":"Thing about Detachment rolls is that Resolve and Composure are about a character's mental and emotional focus and stoicism. For mortals, it makes perfect sense for Integrity, as processing the things they've seen requires them to be steely and in control of their emotions, or rapidly descend. Werewolves sorta fit that, in that their &quot;morality&quot; is swingy, and having a solid sense of self will help them steady their course and keep from falling to extremes. Vampires, on the other hand, are set apart from Humanity, and their actual human self is under constant assault by the Curse, by the receding impact of human needs and experience, and that their own growing experience of humanity as a facade colors their experience of everybody else's humanity. So, a high Willpower definitely helps them maintain the facade, but it doesn't help them retain the empathy and connection that Humanity the trait represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:18:59-07:00","id":467867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467740#post467740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't speak for anyone but myself, but I find that to be a feature, and a big one, not a bug. At character creation, you want to start with a lower Willpower. You want to start with a spiritual Touchstone but not a physical one. You may even want that Merit that increases your bonus from one Touchstone at the cost of the other. Once you hit 5 though, those decisions could backfire on you. You might end up dropping pretty far towards spirit, and need to start taking extreme measures to recover the balance. But you'd better be careful not to over-correct! That back-and forth tension, those dynamic incentives that vary based on how far you are to either side, to me that is exactly what the Harmony balancing act is all about!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have to agree to disagree here, unfortunately. What you describe sounds too much like gaming the system to me. Gimping your character and making other very specific character generation choices to have a decent shot at reaching a good Integrity? That seems to limit character options and overly reward system mastery. We are in agreement about the tension that balancing Harmony should create, though. I just do not like forcing a player to make very specific mechanical choices to get a decent shot at actually partaking in that struggle, instead of just hitting one extreme and then kind of having to deal with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467740#post467740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is admittedly a little counter-intuitive. I agree there may have been a better way to calculate the base dice pool. That said, it's only the sample Breaking Points that cap out at -3. The ST can always create new Breaking Points and/or apply additional penalties based on the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what I would do is simply make the base dice pool a 5 and then go from there. Use more bonuses and penalties depending on circumstances. Going with 5 would mean that a penalty of -3 leaves 2 dice, which is in line with 1e for a severe offense, and Humanity 1 + Touchstone Breaking Points in Requiem (roughly 50/50 chance).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:23:16-07:00","id":467904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467867#post467867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we have to agree to disagree here, unfortunately. What you describe sounds too much like gaming the system to me. Gimping your character and making other very specific character generation choices to have a decent shot at reaching a good Integrity? That seems to limit character options and overly reward system mastery. We are in agreement about the tension that balancing Harmony should create, though. I just do not like forcing a player to make very specific mechanical choices to get a decent shot at actually partaking in that struggle, instead of just hitting one extreme and then kind of having to deal with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it forces specific mechanical choices at all. Those suggestions I gave were of choices one might make for the sake of losing Harmony early on that could lead to problems later on. Alternatively, you could decide that you want to start out with high Willpower and Touchstones on both sides so you'll have the best chances of maintaining Harmony and rely on hitting harsh Breaking Points to achieve balance, though that may have its own consequences. Point is, I like that the system incentivizes different things depending on your Harmony. Sometimes you want Touchstones, sometimes you don't. Sometimes you want to avoid Breaking Points, sometimes you want to actively seek them out. What is beneficial at some Harmony levels may be detrimental at others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466822-getting-harmony-into-balance?p=467867#post467867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what I would do is simply make the base dice pool a 5 and then go from there. Use more bonuses and penalties depending on circumstances. Going with 5 would mean that a penalty of -3 leaves 2 dice, which is in line with 1e for a severe offense, and Humanity 1 + Touchstone Breaking Points in Requiem (roughly 50/50 chance).</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:00:32-07:00","id":468069,"title":"","content":"A lot of the suggestions regarding Touchstones have seemed a little extreme: murdering them, choosing not to have one at all...<br /> My initial question of whether you have to roll aside, do you have to take the Touchstone bonus if it exists in your character's world still? In the chronicle I'm starting up, my character has recently left home to start up with a new pack elsewhere and is trying to keep his contact with his old life to a minimum. Part of his point is to not be in contact with his Touchstones for a time. Not keeping up the relationship seems like it would be enough to drop the bonus; no need to kill the thing/person or waste Merit points making it obsolete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:02:00-07:00","id":468070,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm pretty sure they don't have to be destroyed. Just being distant enough that they stop being a touchstone should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:19:30-07:00","id":468075,"title":"","content":"Dunno... The Hunter in Darkness with a kid he watches over from afar seems like a good physical touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:25:28-07:00","id":468076,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean just physical distance. He watches a kid from afar. If he just stopped, paid no attention to them, put thoughts of them out of his mind, it stands to reason they wouldn't be a touchstone anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:33:01-07:00","id":468083,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure it's just the relationship that matters. Sever ties, and I'd say you lose the bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}